# Agent Instructions — agent-core-kmp

Role: **Supporting (Shared Contracts Library)**
Scope: **Type definitions only — no execution**

## Surface Contract

See: `../../../openspec/specs/client-surfaces/surface-contracts/composeapp-shared.md`

## Contract Scope

This module provides **runtime communication contracts only**:

```kotlin
// In: Surface → Runtime
data class CoreInvocation(
  val prompt: String,
  val sessionId: String? = null,  // UUID, optional
  val metadata: Map<String, String> = emptyMap(),
  val timeoutMs: Long? = null,
)

// Out: Runtime → Surface
data class CoreOutput(
  val text: String,
  val transport: String,
  val rawOutput: String? = null,
)

// Result
sealed interface CoreResult {
  data class Success(val output: CoreOutput) : CoreResult
  data class Failure(...) : CoreResult
}

// Bridge interface
fun interface AgentCoreBridge {
  fun invoke(invocation: CoreInvocation): CoreResult
}
```

## What This Module Is NOT

- **No execution logic** — runtime lives in `clients/agent-runtime`
- **No UI** — UI lives in `clients/composeApp`
- **No state management** — handled by platform targets

## Out of Scope

- HTTP Gateway logic (web-specific)
- CLI direct access (runtime handles this)
- Configuration management
- Session management (CLI bridge handles this)

## Versioning

Contract version: `0.1`
See: `../../../openspec/specs/client-surfaces/spec.md#requirement-contract-layer-scope`

## Adding New Contracts

When adding new contracts:
1. Define in `commonMain` (platform-agnostic)
2. Document in surface contract
3. Update contract version if breaking change
4. Add migration guide if needed
